@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+---
+id: task-005-implement-createpatch-rfc-6902-diff
+type: task
+title: "Implement createPatch RFC 6902 diff"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, instead of the whole
+new version. Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, that returns a JSON Patch
+(RFC 6902) which turns `from` into `to` when applied with the existing `applyPatch`. It must not
+mutate either input, and must describe only what changed — not replace the whole document when a
+small part of it changed.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote failing tests first (`src/index.test.ts`), confirmed they failed because `createPatch` did not
+  exist yet (red), then implemented the function (green).
+- Added `createPatch` to `src/index.ts`: a recursive structural diff over `from`/`to` that reuses the
+  module's existing `deepEqual`, `isMergeableObject` and reference-token escaping. Plain objects diff
+  by key membership (`remove` for a key dropped, `add` for a key gained, recurse for a shared key);
+  arrays diff by common-prefix index with trailing `remove`/`add` for length changes; anything else
+  (a type change, or two unequal scalars) becomes a single `replace`, including at the root pointer
+  `""` when `from`/`to` differ at the top level. Values placed into `add`/`replace` operations are
+  `structuredClone`d so the returned patch cannot alias a value from `to`.
+- The design choices (why structural diff rather than edit-distance/LCS minimization, the array
+  tail-diff strategy, root-replace, cloning, and key-order determinism) are recorded in
+  `dl-004-json-patch-diff-strategy-for-createpatch` (submitted for approval alongside this task).
+- Added tests covering: equal documents (empty patch), scalar and type-changing root replace, a single
+  changed object member leaving the rest of the document out of the patch, added/removed object
+  members, reference-token escaping in generated paths, recursion into nested objects, in-place array
+  element replacement, array append/truncate, a scalar replacing an array (wholesale replace, not an
+  element diff), round-tripping `createPatch` through `applyPatch` to reproduce `to`, non-mutation of
+  both inputs, and non-aliasing of patch values with `to`.
+- Updated `README.md` with a `createPatch` section (signature, behaviour, example), per the
+  documentation directive.
+- Ran `npm run typecheck` (clean) and `npm test` (93/93 passing, including the 14 new `createPatch`
+  tests).
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `createPatch` is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- `applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to))` deep-equals `to` for every tested case, including nested
+  objects, arrays, and root-level type changes.
+- Neither `from` nor `to` is mutated by `createPatch` (test: `does not mutate its inputs`).
+- A single changed field produces a patch with one operation targeting that field, not a replacement
+  of the whole document (test: `describes only the changed member, not the whole document`).
